.*
.* WRKUSRJOB and WRKSBSJOB: the jobs of a user or of a subsystem, with
.* the job options of WRKACTJOB.
:PNLGRP.
:CLASS NAME=OPTCL BASETYPE=ACTION.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=NAMECL BASETYPE='CHAR 10'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=NBRCL BASETYPE='CHAR 6'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=TYPECL BASETYPE='CHAR 7'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=STSCL BASETYPE='CHAR 16'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=FUNCL BASETYPE='CHAR 20'.
:ECLASS.
:VAR NAME=OPT CLASS=OPTCL.
:VAR NAME=JOB CLASS=NAMECL.
:VAR NAME=USER CLASS=NAMECL.
:VAR NAME=NUMBER CLASS=NBRCL.
:VAR NAME=TYPE CLASS=TYPECL.
:VAR NAME=STATUS CLASS=STSCL.
:VAR NAME=FUNCTION CLASS=FUNCL.
:VAR NAME=SBS CLASS=NAMECL.
:VAR NAME=SBSLIB CLASS=NAMECL.
:LISTDEF NAME=JOBS VARS='OPT JOB USER NUMBER TYPE STATUS FUNCTION'.
:KEYL NAME=UJKEYS HELP='KEYS/UJKEYS'.
:KEYI KEY=ENTER ACTION=ENTER.
:KEYI KEY=HELP ACTION=HELP.
:KEYI KEY=PAGEUP ACTION=PAGEUP.
:KEYI KEY=PAGEDOWN ACTION=PAGEDOWN.
:KEYI KEY=F3 ACTION=EXIT.F3=Exit
:KEYI KEY=F4 ACTION='RETURN 4'.F4=Prompt
:KEYI KEY=F5 ACTION='RETURN 5'.F5=Refresh
:KEYI KEY=F9 ACTION=RETRIEVE.F9=Retrieve
:KEYI KEY=F11 ACTION='RETURN 11'.F11=Display schedule data
:KEYI KEY=F12 ACTION=CANCEL.F12=Cancel
:KEYI KEY=F17 ACTION=TOP.F17=Top
:KEYI KEY=F18 ACTION=BOTTOM.F18=Bottom
:KEYI KEY=F21 ACTION='RETURN 21'.F21=Select assistance level
:EKEYL.
:KEYL NAME=SJKEYS HELP='KEYS/SJKEYS'.
:KEYI KEY=ENTER ACTION=ENTER.
:KEYI KEY=HELP ACTION=HELP.
:KEYI KEY=PAGEUP ACTION=PAGEUP.
:KEYI KEY=PAGEDOWN ACTION=PAGEDOWN.
:KEYI KEY=F3 ACTION=EXIT.F3=Exit
:KEYI KEY=F4 ACTION='RETURN 4'.F4=Prompt
:KEYI KEY=F5 ACTION='RETURN 5'.F5=Refresh
:KEYI KEY=F9 ACTION=RETRIEVE.F9=Retrieve
:KEYI KEY=F11 ACTION='RETURN 11'.F11=Display schedule data
:KEYI KEY=F12 ACTION=CANCEL.F12=Cancel
:KEYI KEY=F17 ACTION=TOP.F17=Top
:KEYI KEY=F18 ACTION=BOTTOM.F18=Bottom
:EKEYL.
:PANEL NAME=WRKUSRJOB KEYL=UJKEYS HELP=WRKUSRJOB ENTER='RETURN 1' TOPSEP=DATETIME.Work with User Jobs
:TOPINST.Type options, press Enter.
:LIST DEPTH='*' LISTDEF=JOBS MAXHEAD=2.(No jobs to show)
:LISTACT OPTION=2 ENTER='CMD ?CHGJOB JOB(&NUMBER./&USER./&JOB.)' HELP='WRKUSRJOB/OPTIONS'.2=Change
:LISTACT OPTION=3 ENTER='CMD HLDJOB JOB(&NUMBER./&USER./&JOB.)' HELP='WRKUSRJOB/OPTIONS'.3=Hold
:LISTACT OPTION=4 ENTER='CMD ?ENDJOB JOB(&NUMBER./&USER./&JOB.)' HELP='WRKUSRJOB/OPTIONS'.4=End
:LISTACT OPTION=5 ENTER='CMD WRKJOB JOB(&NUMBER./&USER./&JOB.)' HELP='WRKUSRJOB/OPTIONS'.5=Work with
:LISTACT OPTION=6 ENTER='CMD RLSJOB JOB(&NUMBER./&USER./&JOB.)' HELP='WRKUSRJOB/OPTIONS'.6=Release
:LISTACT OPTION=7 ENTER='CMD DSPJOBLOG JOB(&NUMBER./&USER./&JOB.)' HELP='WRKUSRJOB/OPTIONS'.7=Display message
:LISTACT OPTION=8 ENTER='CMD WRKJOB JOB(&NUMBER./&USER./&JOB.) OPTION(*SPLF)' HELP='WRKUSRJOB/OPTIONS'.8=Work with spooled files
:LISTACT OPTION=13 ENTER='CMD DSCJOB JOB(&NUMBER./&USER./&JOB.)' HELP='WRKUSRJOB/OPTIONS'.13=Disconnect
:LISTCOL VAR=OPT USAGE=INPUT HELP='WRKUSRJOB/OPT'.Opt
:LISTCOL VAR=JOB USAGE=OUTPUT HELP='FLD/JOB'.Job
:LISTCOL VAR=USER USAGE=OUTPUT HELP='FLD/USER'.User
:LISTCOL VAR=TYPE USAGE=OUTPUT HELP='FLD/TYPE'.Type
:LISTCOL VAR=STATUS USAGE=OUTPUT HELP='FLD/STATUS'.-----Status-----
:LISTCOL VAR=FUNCTION USAGE=OUTPUT HELP='FLD/FUNCTION'.Function
:ELIST.
:CMDLINE SIZE=SHORT.
:EPANEL.
:PANEL NAME=WRKSBSJOB KEYL=SJKEYS HELP=WRKSBSJOB ENTER='RETURN 1' TOPSEP=DATETIME.Work with Subsystem Jobs
:DATA DEPTH=2.
:DATAI VAR=SBS USAGE=OUTPUT HELP='FLD/SBS'.Subsystem
.* Not shown: it sets the colon column.
:DATAI VAR=SBSLIB USAGE=OUTPUT DISPLAY=NO.Library of subsystem
:EDATA.
:TOPINST.Type options, press Enter.
:LIST DEPTH='*' LISTDEF=JOBS MAXHEAD=2.(No jobs to show)
:LISTACT OPTION=2 ENTER='CMD ?CHGJOB JOB(&NUMBER./&USER./&JOB.)' HELP='WRKSBSJOB/OPTIONS'.2=Change
:LISTACT OPTION=3 ENTER='CMD HLDJOB JOB(&NUMBER./&USER./&JOB.)' HELP='WRKSBSJOB/OPTIONS'.3=Hold
:LISTACT OPTION=4 ENTER='CMD ?ENDJOB JOB(&NUMBER./&USER./&JOB.)' HELP='WRKSBSJOB/OPTIONS'.4=End
:LISTACT OPTION=5 ENTER='CMD WRKJOB JOB(&NUMBER./&USER./&JOB.)' HELP='WRKSBSJOB/OPTIONS'.5=Work with
:LISTACT OPTION=6 ENTER='CMD RLSJOB JOB(&NUMBER./&USER./&JOB.)' HELP='WRKSBSJOB/OPTIONS'.6=Release
:LISTACT OPTION=7 ENTER='CMD DSPJOBLOG JOB(&NUMBER./&USER./&JOB.)' HELP='WRKSBSJOB/OPTIONS'.7=Display message
:LISTACT OPTION=8 ENTER='CMD WRKJOB JOB(&NUMBER./&USER./&JOB.) OPTION(*SPLF)' HELP='WRKSBSJOB/OPTIONS'.8=Work with spooled files
:LISTACT OPTION=13 ENTER='CMD DSCJOB JOB(&NUMBER./&USER./&JOB.)' HELP='WRKSBSJOB/OPTIONS'.13=Disconnect
:LISTCOL VAR=OPT USAGE=INPUT HELP='WRKSBSJOB/OPT'.Opt
:LISTCOL VAR=JOB USAGE=OUTPUT HELP='FLD/JOB'.Job
:LISTCOL VAR=USER USAGE=OUTPUT HELP='FLD/USER'.User
:LISTCOL VAR=TYPE USAGE=OUTPUT HELP='FLD/TYPE'.Type
:LISTCOL VAR=STATUS USAGE=OUTPUT HELP='FLD/STATUS'.-----Status-----
:LISTCOL VAR=FUNCTION USAGE=OUTPUT HELP='FLD/FUNCTION'.Function
:ELIST.
:CMDLINE SIZE=SHORT.
:EPANEL.
:HELP NAME=WRKUSRJOB.Work with User Jobs - Help
:P.The jobs a user profile runs: active ones, ones waiting on a job
queue and ones that ended with spooled output left. Type an option
next to a job, or a command on the command line.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=WRKSBSJOB.Work with Subsystem Jobs - Help
:P.The jobs running in a subsystem, or in every active subsystem.
Type an option next to a job, or a command on the command line.
:EHELP.
.* Item, key and option help.
:HELP NAME='KEYS/UJKEYS'.Function keys
:PARML.
:PT.F3=Exit
:PD.Ends the display and returns to where it was started from.
:PT.F4=Prompt
:PD.Prompts the command on the command line, or the command of the
option typed.
:PT.F5=Refresh
:PD.Shows the display again with the current information.
:PT.F9=Retrieve
:PD.Puts the last command run back on the command line; press it again
for the one before.
:PT.F11=Display schedule data
:PD.Display schedule data.
:PT.F12=Cancel
:PD.Returns to the previous display without acting on what was typed.
:PT.F17=Top
:PD.Moves to the top of the list.
:PT.F18=Bottom
:PD.Moves to the bottom of the list.
:PT.F21=Select assistance level
:PD.Select assistance level.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKUSRJOB/OPT'.Option
:P.Type the number of an option next to an entry and press Enter. The
options the list allows are shown above it; F1 on one of them explains
it.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/JOB'.Job
:P.The job, by name, user and number. A job name alone is enough when
only one job has it.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/USER'.User
:P.The user of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/TYPE'.Type
:P.The type of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/STATUS'.-----Status-----
:P.The -----Status----- of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/FUNCTION'.Function
:P.The function of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKUSRJOB/OPTIONS'.Options
:P.Type an option number next to one or more entries and press Enter.
The option runs for each entry it is typed next to, in order.
:PARML.
:PT.2=Change
:PD.Type 2 next to an entry and press Enter to change it. The Change Job
(CHGJOB) command is prompted for the entry.
:PT.3=Hold
:PD.Type 3 next to an entry and press Enter to hold it. The Hold Job
(HLDJOB) command runs for the entry.
:PT.4=End
:PD.Type 4 next to an entry and press Enter to end it. The End Job
(ENDJOB) command is prompted for the entry.
:PT.5=Work with
:PD.Type 5 next to an entry and press Enter to work with it. The Work
with Job (WRKJOB) command runs for the entry.
:PT.6=Release
:PD.Type 6 next to an entry and press Enter to release it. The Release
Job (RLSJOB) command runs for the entry.
:PT.7=Display message
:PD.Type 7 next to an entry and press Enter to display message it. The
Display Job Log (DSPJOBLOG) command runs for the entry.
:PT.8=Work with spooled files
:PD.Type 8 next to an entry and press Enter to work with spooled files
it. The Work with Job (WRKJOB) command runs for the entry.
:PT.13=Disconnect
:PD.Type 13 next to an entry and press Enter to disconnect it. The
Disconnect Job (DSCJOB) command runs for the entry.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='KEYS/SJKEYS'.Function keys
:PARML.
:PT.F3=Exit
:PD.Ends the display and returns to where it was started from.
:PT.F4=Prompt
:PD.Prompts the command on the command line, or the command of the
option typed.
:PT.F5=Refresh
:PD.Shows the display again with the current information.
:PT.F9=Retrieve
:PD.Puts the last command run back on the command line; press it again
for the one before.
:PT.F11=Display schedule data
:PD.Display schedule data.
:PT.F12=Cancel
:PD.Returns to the previous display without acting on what was typed.
:PT.F17=Top
:PD.Moves to the top of the list.
:PT.F18=Bottom
:PD.Moves to the bottom of the list.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/SBS'.Subsystem
:P.The subsystem shown for what the display is about.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKSBSJOB/OPT'.Option
:P.Type the number of an option next to an entry and press Enter. The
options the list allows are shown above it; F1 on one of them explains
it.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKSBSJOB/OPTIONS'.Options
:P.Type an option number next to one or more entries and press Enter.
The option runs for each entry it is typed next to, in order.
:PARML.
:PT.2=Change
:PD.Type 2 next to an entry and press Enter to change it. The Change Job
(CHGJOB) command is prompted for the entry.
:PT.3=Hold
:PD.Type 3 next to an entry and press Enter to hold it. The Hold Job
(HLDJOB) command runs for the entry.
:PT.4=End
:PD.Type 4 next to an entry and press Enter to end it. The End Job
(ENDJOB) command is prompted for the entry.
:PT.5=Work with
:PD.Type 5 next to an entry and press Enter to work with it. The Work
with Job (WRKJOB) command runs for the entry.
:PT.6=Release
:PD.Type 6 next to an entry and press Enter to release it. The Release
Job (RLSJOB) command runs for the entry.
:PT.7=Display message
:PD.Type 7 next to an entry and press Enter to display message it. The
Display Job Log (DSPJOBLOG) command runs for the entry.
:PT.8=Work with spooled files
:PD.Type 8 next to an entry and press Enter to work with spooled files
it. The Work with Job (WRKJOB) command runs for the entry.
:PT.13=Disconnect
:PD.Type 13 next to an entry and press Enter to disconnect it. The
Disconnect Job (DSCJOB) command runs for the entry.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:EPNLGRP.
